---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import CtaBand from "../components/CtaBand.astro";
import sloveniaImg from "../assets/from-wp/countryside-meadow.webp";
import kitchenImg from "../assets/from-wp/kitchen-board.webp";
import familyImg from "../assets/from-wp/couple.webp";
import wordmarkImg from "../assets/from-wp/fitfambam-wordmark.webp";
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="FitFamBam is Luka and Mariah Dolenc’s family journal in Slovenia. What it is, and what it is not."
>
  <header class="page-hero wrap">
    <p class="kicker">About</p>
    <h1>A family in <span class="accent">Slovenia.</span> A page with a name.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      We are Luka and Mariah Dolenc. We live in Slovenia with our four children. FitFamBam is ours together. It is personal. It is not a club.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="feature">
    <Image src={sloveniaImg} alt="A sunny meadow and woods in the countryside" widths={[800, 1200, 1600]} sizes="100vw" quality={72} format="webp" />
    <p class="cap wrap">From the old site archive. A meadow near home, not a stock lake.</p>
  </div>

  <Section eyebrow="The short version" title="What FitFamBam" accent="is.">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        A family journal and a calling card. Movement, food, rest, and the people we live with. We want to stay capable for a long time, in a house that is already full.
      </p>
      <p>
        We married in 2011. Mariah left California the next morning and has been here since. In 2015 we had two daughters, Olivia and Leia. We now have four children.
      </p>
      <p>
        The name is ours. The later domain is FitFamBam.com. Until then, this static site is the whole thing.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <div class="split wrap">
    <figure>
      <Image src={kitchenImg} alt="Tomato, avocado, and cheese on seeded bread" widths={[640, 1000]} sizes="(min-width: 800px) 45vw, 90vw" quality={70} format="webp" />
    </figure>
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">What it is not</p>
      <h2>No memberships. <span class="accent">No miracle week.</span></h2>
      <ul class="not-list">
        <li>Not a gym with classes and a desk at the door.</li>
        <li>Not a shop, and not a catalogue of products.</li>
        <li>Not medical advice. We are parents writing about a household, not clinicians.</li>
        <li>Not a transformation brand. Bodies change slowly, in private.</li>
        <li>Not a staff of trainers. You will not find invented names here.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Section tone="soft" eyebrow="How we live" title="A full house." accent="A small country.">
    <div class="two">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Slovenia is the right size for this. You can walk into trees from a lot of front doors. The food is close. Sunday still means something.
        </p>
        <p>
          Mariah sees space, type, and colour before Luka does. She liked a polished gym look we once tried, and could not bend it. FitFamBam is built so she can restyle it from one file. If the accent should shift, we change a token. The pages follow.
        </p>
        <p>
          Photographs on these pages are ours from the old archive: a meadow, a kitchen board, the two of us, a couple of beaches. Photos of the children live in the archive folder and are not used here.
        </p>
      </div>
      <figure>
        <Image src={familyImg} alt="Luka and Mariah, a close portrait" widths={[640, 1000]} sizes="(min-width: 800px) 40vw, 90vw" quality={70} format="webp" />
      </figure>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="The journal" title="Mariah wrote first." accent="Luka writes when he can.">
    <div class="archive-split">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          In 2015 Mariah kept a FitFamBam journal: garden dirt, rice-cake sandwiches, pregnancy, Ljubljana. Those posts are back, marked as archive, with her name on them. Luka did not write them.
        </p>
        <p>
          Luka’s first new note is only this: the site is ours again, and he will add to it when there is a sentence worth keeping.
        </p>
        <p>
          The old photo wordmark below is how the name looked then. Thin white caps on bokeh. The mark in the header is the one we use now.
        </p>
        <a class="btn" href="/journal">Read the journal</a>
      </div>
      <figure class="wordmark-hist">
        <Image src={wordmarkImg} alt="The 2015 FitFamBam wordmark, type over a bokeh photograph" widths={[640, 1000]} sizes="(min-width: 800px) 40vw, 90vw" quality={70} format="webp" />
        <figcaption>Historical mark from the 2015 site. Not the live logo.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <CtaBand title="If this feels like your kind of" accent="quiet," />
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    padding: var(--space-3xl) 0 var(--space-xl);
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    max-width: 18ch;
    margin: 0.3em 0 0.5em;
  }

  .feature {
    padding-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .feature :global(img) {
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 8;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .cap {
    margin: 0.75rem auto 0;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: var(--step-small);
  }

  .split,
  .two,
  .archive-split {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);
    align-items: center;
    padding-bottom: var(--space-3xl);
  }

  .archive-split {
    padding-bottom: 0;
  }

  figure {
    margin: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  figure :global(img) {
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .wordmark-hist {
    background: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .wordmark-hist :global(img) {
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 10;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .wordmark-hist figcaption {
    padding: 0.75rem 0.2rem 0;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: var(--step-small);
    background: var(--color-paper);
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    margin: 0.3em 0 0.8em;
  }

  .not-list {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .not-list li {
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    position: relative;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .not-list li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.55em;
    width: 0.45rem;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--color-accent);
  }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .split,
    .two,
    .archive-split {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .feature :global(img),
    figure :global(img) {
      aspect-ratio: 16 / 10;
    }
  }
</style>
